Message-ID: <pBUsVMEXUDg.0mF8yeOlBQAJ@shinyapps-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <pBUsVMEXUDg.R8r761j0BgAJ@shinyapps-users.groups.google.com>
References: <pBUsVMEXUDg.R8r761j0BgAJ@shinyapps-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shinyapps-users/c/pBUsVMEXUDg/m/0mF8yeOlBQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

We serve a robots.txt to prevent crawlers from trying to index because we found that they would cause applications to start up, but they would not actually perform the subsequent Ajax requests that would render content worthy of them indexing.

We have captured a feature on our backlog to allow for the creation of static content for an application that would be served to crawlers, but this work is not scheduled at this time.

On Thursday, February 16, 2017 at 9:43:13 PM UTC-5, Will Phillips wrote:
> Hello,
>
> I'm just starting out with Shiny and a basic account.  I was wondering if search engines like Google will index the app pages I post on my account in shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>.  If they will, does anyone know of a command or function to include in my shiny code to keep them from doing this?
>
> Will

